WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.580
Most of the time we hear without really listening.

2
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.740
When we sit still and listen, the backyard fills up with sounds.

3
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.000
Ears catch them like funnels, and cupped hands make a bigger funnel.

4
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:20.793
You need paper and crayons or pencils, a timer, such as a phone, and a towel or mat

5
00:00:20.793 --> 00:00:21.793
to sit on outside.

6
00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:25.227
Pick a quiet spot away from roads and water.

7
00:00:26.187 --> 00:00:29.327
Ask how many sounds your child expects, and write the number down.

8
00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:31.427
Set the timer for two minutes.

9
00:00:32.307 --> 00:00:36.107
Your child closes their eyes and holds up one finger for each new sound.

10
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.520
Expect anything from a few sounds to a dozen or more.

11
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.740
Then your child cups both hands behind the ears.

12
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:45.840
Most children hear it louder.

13
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.540
Cupped hands catch more sound, like a cat's big ears.

14
00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.043
Stay close enough to touch.

15
00:00:52.043 --> 00:00:56.643
Cup hands only for quiet or everyday sounds, never toward a road.

16
00:00:57.363 --> 00:00:58.723
Nothing goes into the ear.
